<title>USA: Mass. top court rules policyholders get $176 mln.</title>
<headline>Mass. top court rules policyholders get $176 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts highest state court ruled on Wednesday that auto insurance companies must refund over charges totaling $176 million to policyholders in the state.</p>
<p>The Supreme Judicial Court ruling gives insurance companies three years to refund the money to policyholders who can expect to get about $60 back, according to Massachusetts Insurance Commissioner Linda Ruthardt.</p>
<p>A worker at the state division of insurance discovered a mathematical mistake last year in the way insurers calculated their expenses.</p>
<p>((--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106))</p>
</text>
